(Success). New curated helpers: Hrot.AI.Behaviors.Brains.SegmentMath.LerpParam/Lerp (the count\u003E1?i/(count-1):0.5 ternary and the a\u002B(b-a)*t interpolation -- no visual-node form for the conditional, architect Q#6-A), Hrot.AI.Behaviors.Brains.MoveIntentJson.Build (curated JSON-payload builder for the MoveToLocationParams DTO, architect Q#6-C -- serialization stays in reviewable C#, the graph only publishes the resulting string), Hrot.AI.Behaviors.Brains.MaskOps.WithBitSet (bitwise mask-set \u002B the i\u003C16 guard, architect Q#6-A -- bitwise ops have no visual-node form). Reuses Hrot.AI.Behaviors.Brains.WorldOps.IsAlive (P7 context-aware FunctionCall, already introduced by the AimAndFireSpecific slice). DEVIATION 1 (documented): the oracle\u0027s leading \u0027if (!HasComponent\u003CUnitRoster\u003E(Self)) return Success\u0027 guard is omitted -- the FlowForEach lowering reads GetComponentRO\u003CUnitRoster\u003E on self unconditionally, exactly as HillAssault2_AreAllAtBaseline already does (the commander always has a UnitRoster in practice; the proof test adds it explicitly). DEVIATION 2 (documented): the oracle\u0027s BehaviorLog.IsDebugEnabled diagnostic logging calls are not reproduced (debug-only side channel, no bearing on WorkingState/return-status/published-event behavior). Does not modify the C# oracle (HillAttackCommanderNodes.Action_DispatchAllToBaseline).",
